    "why": "Implication is false in exactly one row: antecedent true and consequent false. Every other row is true, including rows where the antecedent is false.",
    "counterexample": "q -> (not p and (p or q)) looks like the tautology above but is false at p = true, q = true: the right side becomes (false and true) = false, so true -> false = false."
